<h1>Latest News</h1>

<h2>CCIA submission to Ontario's Data Centre Playbook consultation</h2>

<p>The CCIA's work on data-centre development involves communities and municipal actors across
Ontario and the country. While specific local circumstances can differ, the underlying governance
issue is the same. Municipalities are being asked to assess large infrastructure projects of a novel
nature even while existing standards and frameworks remain non-enforceable, incomplete, and
outdated. Project information is often fragmented or opaque, making local costs and benefits difficult
to assess and verify.</p>

<p>We welcome Ontario's decision to develop a provincial Data Centre Playbook. For the framework to
succeed, it must treat municipalities as governments with independent authority over host-community
impacts, not as mere stakeholders to be consulted only after major investment and grid decisions
have already been made.</p>

<p>Read our full submission <a href="../files/Ontario_Data-Centre-Playbook-Submission_CCIA-AICC.pdf" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
